WEBVTT

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.799 --> 00:00:05.733
Today we talk about the part of the job that clients rarely notice,

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:08.110
but good technicians take very seriously:

00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:10.110
refills, and removal.

00:00:10.699 --> 00:00:12.670
Applying a beautiful set is one thing.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:18.030
Keeping her natural lashes healthy over many months, many years, is something else.

00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:22.350
And most of that comes down to how you do refills, and how you do removals.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:26.849
First, recall the life cycle of a lash, from the classic lesson.

00:00:27.397 --> 00:00:30.114
Every day, a few natural lashes shed naturally,

00:00:30.064 --> 00:00:33.009
and the extensions attached to them fall with them.

00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:37.809
Meanwhile, other lashes grow longer, pushing the bond away from the eyelid.

00:00:38.158 --> 00:00:41.009
And new baby lashes grow in, with no extension yet.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:45.362
After about two to three weeks, the set looks sparser, with gaps,

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.649
and some grown out lashes sticking out.

00:00:47.935 --> 00:00:49.889
That is when the client needs a refill.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.057
Refills are usually every two to three weeks,

00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:57.830
depending on how fast each person sheds, and how the client looks after her lashes.

00:00:58.165 --> 00:01:03.168
Leave it too long, and too few lashes remain, many have grown long and twisted,

00:01:03.118 --> 00:01:05.990
and the refill becomes almost a full new set.

00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:08.070
Each salon sets its own rule:

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:10.550
how long a gap still counts as a refill.

00:01:10.793 --> 00:01:14.790
Booking the refill as soon as the client finishes her set is the simplest way.

00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:19.048
Every refill is also a chance to read the lashes like a diary.

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:24.168
Lashes lost mostly from one eye usually mean the client sleeps on that side.

00:01:24.698 --> 00:01:28.059
Losing a whole patch at the outer corner can come from rubbing,

00:01:28.009 --> 00:01:29.688
or from an oily makeup remover.

00:01:30.114 --> 00:01:33.962
Even loss all over, and you should check the glue, the room humidity,

00:01:33.912 --> 00:01:36.328
and how the lashes were cleansed last time.

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:40.168
Ask the client, look closely, then write it in the profile.

00:01:40.349 --> 00:01:43.608
Find the cause, and next time the lashes last longer.

00:01:44.286 --> 00:01:46.987
At a refill, which extensions do you remove?

00:01:47.464 --> 00:01:49.387
First, the ones that have grown out:

00:01:49.654 --> 00:01:54.036
the bond sits far from the eyelid, and the extension has turned sideways,

00:01:53.986 --> 00:01:56.587
sticks out, or crosses the lash next to it.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:01.173
Left in place, it looks bad, and it weighs on the tip of the natural lash,

00:02:01.123 --> 00:02:02.507
pulling and twisting it.

00:02:02.926 --> 00:02:04.747
Second, any stickies.

00:02:05.082 --> 00:02:08.827
Third, extensions that are loose, and not firmly attached.

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:13.627
Extensions that still look good, and still sit close to the lid, stay.

00:02:14.182 --> 00:02:16.583
Now the most important point of the lesson today:

00:02:16.842 --> 00:02:20.103
never pull, yank or pluck an extension off.

00:02:20.609 --> 00:02:23.863
The glue holds the extension firmly on the natural lash.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.045
So pulling the extension pulls the natural lash out of its follicle too,

00:02:27.995 --> 00:02:28.903
before its time.

00:02:29.427 --> 00:02:32.503
Do it again and again, and the follicles are damaged:

00:02:32.693 --> 00:02:36.583
lashes grow back sparser and weaker, and sometimes not at all.

00:02:36.762 --> 00:02:39.463
The same goes for clients picking at their lashes at home.

00:02:39.636 --> 00:02:41.383
So tell the client very clearly:

00:02:41.732 --> 00:02:46.023
even if a lash feels caught, never remove it yourself, come back to the salon.

00:02:46.538 --> 00:02:51.324
To remove an extension, first soften the glue with a professional lash remover,

00:02:51.274 --> 00:02:54.021
and only then slide the extension off gently.

00:02:54.686 --> 00:02:56.181
Another thing that happens a lot:

00:02:56.474 --> 00:03:01.621
some people use oil, like an oily makeup remover, to dissolve the glue near the eye.

00:03:02.038 --> 00:03:05.541
Never do that, unless the product maker clearly says so.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:10.787
Oil weakens the glue unevenly, is hard to control, spreads easily into the eye,

00:03:10.737 --> 00:03:14.661
and leaves a film that makes the next application bond poorly.

00:03:15.173 --> 00:03:17.377
Lash removers come in several forms.

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:20.939
The cream type and the thick gel type stay where you put them,

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:23.137
so they are easier to control near the eye.

00:03:23.556 --> 00:03:26.977
The liquid type runs more easily, so you have to be very careful.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:30.017
Whatever the type, follow the maker's instructions:

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.857
how much to apply, how long to wait, and what to wipe with.

00:03:34.206 --> 00:03:35.937
And a rule with no exceptions:

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:38.177
remover must never get into the eye.

00:03:38.521 --> 00:03:41.617
The client's eyes stay fully closed during removal.

00:03:42.015 --> 00:03:45.259
If she feels stinging, stop at once, wipe off the remover,

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:48.177
and handle it as in the lesson on handling incidents.

00:03:48.753 --> 00:03:50.818
So when do you remove the whole set?

00:03:51.206 --> 00:03:54.645
When retention is poor, the lashes fall out unevenly,

00:03:54.595 --> 00:03:57.778
and refill after refill still does not look good.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.718
When the client wants to give her lashes a break,

00:04:00.668 --> 00:04:02.578
or does not want extensions any more.

00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:04.578
When the client has a reaction:

00:04:04.736 --> 00:04:08.850
red, swollen or itchy eyes after the service, remove everything,

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.818
and advise her to see a doctor.

00:04:11.076 --> 00:04:15.438
And after many refills in a row, when the set has become messy and uneven,

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:19.458
removing it and starting fresh is better than forcing another refill.

00:04:20.196 --> 00:04:21.054
After removal,

00:04:21.004 --> 00:04:25.557
the natural lashes usually look sparser and shorter than the client remembers.

00:04:26.063 --> 00:04:28.169
That is not because removal damaged them,

00:04:28.119 --> 00:04:30.677
but because she has got used to seeing extensions.

00:04:31.222 --> 00:04:35.077
Tell her this beforehand, very gently, so she does not panic.

00:04:35.506 --> 00:04:37.791
And never remove half a set and leave it,

00:04:37.741 --> 00:04:40.517
or tell the client to remove them herself at home,

00:04:40.626 --> 00:04:42.277
with oil or with her fingers.

00:04:42.524 --> 00:04:45.477
If she wants them removed, invite her back to the salon.

00:04:45.982 --> 00:04:48.353
A proper removal takes only a short while,

00:04:48.303 --> 00:04:52.277
but a wrong removal at home can cost her a whole row of natural lashes.

00:04:52.912 --> 00:04:55.840
Finally, teach the client how to care for her lashes,

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.773
because most early shedding comes from habits at home.

00:04:59.178 --> 00:05:00.932
No rubbing, no picking.

00:05:01.275 --> 00:05:03.093
Oil free products around the eyes.

00:05:03.566 --> 00:05:07.573
Wash the lashes gently, and brush them every day with a clean wand.

00:05:07.988 --> 00:05:12.933
No lash curler, and no waterproof mascara, because it is very hard to remove.

00:05:13.344 --> 00:05:17.573
Sleep on her back, or slightly on her side, not face down in the pillow.

00:05:17.876 --> 00:05:21.312
When the client cares for her lashes well, refills are easier,

00:05:21.262 --> 00:05:23.333
and her natural lashes are healthier.

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:24.692
So you see.

00:05:25.014 --> 00:05:27.572
Refills and removal are not a side job.

00:05:28.002 --> 00:05:31.252
They are the reason clients trust your salon for the long term.

00:05:31.508 --> 00:05:35.795
No pulling, no yanking, remover in the right place for the right time,

00:05:35.745 --> 00:05:37.732
and clear advice for the client.

00:05:38.135 --> 00:05:40.038
When her natural lashes stay healthy,

00:05:39.988 --> 00:05:43.092
the client will keep coming back to you for a very long time.

00:05:43.439 --> 00:05:46.852
In the practice lesson, we will go through it step by step together.

00:05:47.101 --> 00:05:49.492
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:49.818 --> 00:05:50.532
See you next time.
